Package: BrainNetTest
Title: Statistical Testing and Edge Identification in Brain Network Populations
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Maximiliano", "Martino", , "maxii.martino@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: BrainNetTest provides tools for analyzing and statistically 
    testing brain networks represented as graphs. Each brain is modeled as 
    an undirected graph where nodes correspond to brain regions and edges 
    to functional or structural connections. The package implements:
    (i) computation of central (representative) graphs and distances between 
    networks, 
    (ii) statistical hypothesis testing for global population differences 
    using the T statistic, 
    (iii) edge-level inference via Fisher’s exact test, chi-squared tests, or 
    proportion tests, including multiple testing corrections, 
    (iv) ranking and visualization of significant edges, and 
    (v) an iterative algorithm to identify critical connections responsible 
    for inter-population differences. 
    Applications include neuroscientific studies aiming to distinguish 
    populations (e.g., control vs diseased) and to highlight the specific 
    brain connections driving observed differences.
